  "text": "Track 5.1 Is it a good thing that football is such a big business these days? I'm talking to club manager Victor Romanov and player Obi Kanu who has just signed a contract with Westchester United Congratulations, Obi. Thank you Let's start with Victor Victor you've been a club manager for 30 years. Do you think that there is too much money in football? Well, yes and no People are happy to spend lots of money on what they love in my opinion if there is a lot of money in football, it's because of the fans and This is great because clubs can pay for players to have the best training So they have more skills and get better and better Today's players are the best ever Okay, so football players these days are very good But the salaries they earn are still too much and the cost of tickets is too high Clubs charge so much money that many fans can't afford to come to matches Okay, but fans can still watch the game on television A lot of money comes from television and advertising Clubs need that money very much The clubs often have money problems and the club managers worry about this more than anybody else We always have to make more money so we can attract champion players who will score goals and help us win matches Without those players clubs cannot continue So Obie you trained at the famous Abidjan football academy in the Ivory Coast What's your opinion of football as a business? Well, the Ivory Coast is not a rich country I spent all my time as a kid kicking a football around with my friends in the streets We all dreamed of getting into the academy It's the one big chance to make money We had to compete with each other all the time The big prize is getting into a professional team Then you can support your family and give them a better life But you have to work hard and be strong. You also have to be lucky to get the opportunity The football business is hardest of all for the players Clubs are businesses that buy and sell us if you get hurt and can't play anymore You can lose your job Nobody cares about you after that",
